ebase] so the completion verifier accepts a recorded attestation instead of failing to find code proof.","AC item '- [ ] AC5 [non-codebase] - After an operator `terraform apply`, `aws logs tail /rebar/gerrit-host --' carries a [non-codebase] tag that is not at the start of the checkbox text, so it is treated as untagged and judged by the codebase bar. Move the tag to the start of the checkbox text (`- [ ] [non-codebase] <criterion>`), or put a mere mention of the tag in backticks.","AC item '- [ ] AC6 [non-codebase] - The Route 53 health check reports Healthy, and its alarm is OK while Gerr' carries a [non-codebase] tag that is not at the start of the checkbox text, so it is treated as untagged and judged by the codebase bar. Move the tag to the start of the checkbox text (`- [ ] [non-codebase] <criterion>`), or put a mere mention of the tag in backticks."],"finding":"Acceptance-criteria / definition-of-done quality issues.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f607dd457c67f9209","impact":0.4,"is_primary":null,"location":"","norm_id":"ned06ebc801a522e3","priority":0.4,"reason":null,"recalled":false,"scenarios":[],"severity":"minor","suggested_fix":"Split compound criteria, replace subjective terms with observable outcomes, and state how each is verified.","tier":"DET","validity":1.0,"verification":null},{"block_threshold":0.8,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] State in the plan (and runbook evidence section) that the on-box CloudWatch agent cannot be relied on to ship the final run-up during a root-disk-100% wedge, name the console capture + Route53 check + IncomingLogEvents alarm as the backstops for that terminal window, and soften AC4/runbook claims that off-box logs capture 'the last seconds before the host went quiet'.","cohort":["G6"],"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.8,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Context names the failure as a host that 'dies with it' and the runbook under review attributes the 2026-09-04 class to a root volume at 100% that kills the SSM agent and the on-box probe ('at 100% the SSM agent dies along with everything else')","The CloudWatch agent is itself an on-box process reading journald and buffering locally; at 100% root disk, journald stops accepting writes and the agent cannot advance/ship, so the final run-up may never leave the box","Runbook text 'Everything the host already logged is off-box in CloudWatch Logs ... and survives the restart' is true only for data already shipped before the wedge, not the terminal window the plan elsewhere claims to preserve ('the last seconds before the host went quiet')"],"finding":"The forensic goal ('capture what the host did in the last seconds before it went quiet') is served by an on-box shipper (CloudWatch agent) in a failure mode (root disk filling to 100%) that disables on-box processes; the plan overstates terminal-window coverage and does not state this residual gap.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f8b9dd6b9f7fae409","impact":0.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach / Config content; AC4/AC5; host_logs.tf shipping-stopped alarm","norm_id":"ne51791eebbf06a7d","priority":0.0,"reason":"low-validity","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A future root-disk-full wedge identical to 2026-09-04: operator opens /rebar/gerrit-host expecting the final minutes and finds the stream truncated at the point shipping stalled, mirroring the original evidence gap"],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.3333,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"no","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"no","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes